The existing F17 two-summand factor-base system has two better canonical presentations:
XOR recoding gives exact degree 6 with seven variables, and one-hot support gives exact degree 5 with nine variables. The original labels give degree 7; the same-base dense presentation gives degree 9. All selector variables and support constraints are counted.

#text(weight: "bold")[Identity.] `icv1-fp5-tm1-a77cc6af`, curve `y^2=x^3+2x+2` over F17; `FB1h29cc024e755c`. Eight columns, sixteen signed points. Reuse the original issuer and FB1 dump. This is a new presentation of the same points, with no newly registered curve.

