#pagebreak()
= Algebra and exact semantics

#text(weight: "bold")[1. XOR.] Boolean replacement `(u,v) → (u+v-2u v,v)` is an involution. The offset becomes `2u+12v-4u v` and retains exactly `{0,2,10,12}`. The two graph equations and four Boolean equations remain in the seven-variable system.

After invertible row normalization, the top ideal is generated by
`m^2`, `x z`, `x^2-a m x-u v`, `z^2-b m z-w t`, and the four bit squares.
Every degree-6 monomial vanishes. The functional with support
`x m u v w`, `x^2u v w`, `x^3m w`, `x^4w` and weights `1,a,1,2a` annihilates the ideal but takes value 1 on the degree-5 witness `x^3m w`. Both bounds are checked over a field. `RecodedCanonical.lean` connects this ideal to the actual generator set; `FourTrackFixture.lean` instantiates the F17 system and complete finite-target point semantics.

#text(weight: "bold")[2. One-hot.] Three bits per slot satisfy Boolean equations and all same-slot pair products. Exactly 000, 100, 010, 001 remain; weights 2, 10, 12 give the original offsets. At most one bit per slot survives in the top quotient. Together with degree-3 core vanishing this gives the degree-5 upper bound. Retaining one bit per slot maps to the old two-bit quotient; its degree-4 witness remains nonzero when characteristic is not 2. `SupportOneHot.lean` checks both bounds and the actual highest-form bridge.

#text(weight: "bold")[3. Symmetric chord.] Set `σ=m^2-r`, `π=r^2+r m^2+A+2m s`, and `D=σ^2-4π`. Recover `x=(σ+d)/2`, `z=(σ-d)/2`. Two incidence equations are linear in `d`, with `d^2=D`. `SymmetricChord.lean` proves equivalence and covers three disjoint cases: first pivot nonzero; first zero and second nonzero; both zero with both constants zero and a square root in the base field. The six-variable native system retains `d`; no saturated chart is counted as a complete search. Its canonical degree remains open.

#text(weight: "bold")[4. Determinant.] A 3×3 pencil with bottom-right identity block has determinant `y-(a x^2+b x+c+l_0+l_1l_2)`. Its normalized kernel is `[1,-a x,-l_2]`. This chart is complete. Choosing `l_0=2u+12v`, `l_1=-4u`, `l_2=v` returns XOR membership. `Determinantal.lean` checks the equivalence.

The expanded 13-variable system loses both ordinate variables from its highest forms. Evaluation sending one ordinate to 1 and all other variables to 0 annihilates the whole top ideal but every power of that ordinate maps to 1. `DeterminantalTop.lean` proves no finite homogeneous first vanishing, including arbitrary affine lower terms. This does not assert that its affine solution set is infinite. Schur elimination returns the seven-variable XOR system; it is a separately priced reduction.

