= Checks, sources and next experiment

The native Rust implementation emits all six model families. The known-answer target (13,10) yields 21 complete inputs, with msolve syntax, sparse F17 polynomial coefficients, exact ordered group references and hashes. Uncompressed metadata SHA256:
#text(size: 8pt)[`154c40dcea500bfe76a7eb9d8bb411e42e4106407d0ad6bf909a7b8528d7c87c`]

Seven release correctness tests check arithmetic, unchanged labels/points, complete scalar reference against group replay on all 18 finite targets, symmetric and determinantal evaluations, dense/group equivalence, every F17 linear-square pivot case, and one-hot support with group replay. Correctness-test harness time is not a benchmark. All performance/rank counters in the export are null.

`verify.sh` checks source hashes, the Lake project, warnings-as-errors, the unchanged whole transitive axiom auditor, native clippy/formatting/tests and byte-identical fixed-fixture export. Lean is pinned to 4.19.0 and Mathlib to `c44e0c8ee63ca166450922a373c7409c5d26b00b`. The source-linked Markdown report, proof map and `verification/` receipts are the detailed record. Failed development logs and source snapshots are retained separately from accepted sources; no sorry, custom axiom or native trust is accepted.

The broad root-library attempt under installed Rust 1.94.1 reaches the two existing E0658 `atomic_try_update` errors in `src/cryptanalysis/ecbench/pencil.rs` and `src/cryptanalysis/ecbench/diagnostic_runtime.rs`. No unrelated source workaround or root-library pass is claimed. Use a compatible root toolchain and current-head CI for that scope.

#text(weight: "bold")[Prospective comparison.] `PROTOCOL.md` freezes a complete finite-target panel, all four signs, exact decoding/replay, A/A controls and all setup/branch/reconstruction work. It requires matched msolve F4 and the fastest licensed reference when available, with matrix dimensions, degrees, arithmetic, RAM and disk counters. No new CAS/time/yield experiment has launched. The current EKS route lacks an arbitrary standalone CAS adapter and ready identity; host and budget admission remain to be frozen. Original 17-term P-256 gates remain separate obligations.

